      "content": "That relentless need to perform \"normalcy\" while feeling utterly drained is a form of toxic burnout that leaves no room for genuine repair. When masking your pain requires its own massive energy cost, any moment of true rest feels like another impossible task one can't commit to doing. Please try to be gentle with yourself today and allow yourself to simply exist without having to climb that mountain again.",
      "source": "target",
